#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:1
msgid "Deployment Cookbook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:3
msgid ""
"This page gives practical defaults for choosing CPU offload, FSDP, CFG "
"parallelism, SP, and TP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:5
msgid "Quick Rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:7
msgid "Use the simplest setting that fits your memory target:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Goal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Recommended setting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Fastest single-GPU run when the model fits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Disable CPU offload and do not use FSDP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Lower single-GPU memory usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid ""
"Use component CPU offload, or layerwise DiT offload for supported Wan/MOVA "
"models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Faster multi-GPU Qwen/Wan CFG generation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Use FSDP with CFG parallelism and disable CPU offload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Sequence length or video-shape scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Use SP/Ulysses/Ring when the model benefits from sequence parallelism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "TP compatibility or encoder-heavy paths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Set TP explicitly; do not treat TP as the default latency optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:17
msgid "Base the decision on available memory on the selected GPU(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:19
msgid ""
"For multi-GPU deployment: the least-free selected GPU is the bottleneck. A "
"busy 80GiB GPU can behave like a much smaller GPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:20
msgid ""
"For single-GPU deployment: FSDP shards DiT weights across multiple GPUs. It "
"is not useful for keeping a single-GPU deployment on one GPU; for that case "
"use CPU offload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:22
msgid "Performance Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:24
msgid ""
"`--performance-mode` applies safe presets without overriding explicit "
"offload, FSDP, or parallelism flags. `auto` is the default. Use `manual` "
"when you need to keep performance-related server args under explicit user "
"control. `--mode` is a short alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "`manual`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "Keeps performance-related server args under explicit user control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "`auto`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid ""
"Default. Keeps legacy safe offload defaults and uses FSDP/CFG only on "
"validated multi-GPU deployments where FSDP can replace DiT offload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "`speed`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid ""
"Favors GPU-resident execution for lower latency and higher throughput. "
"Disables CPU offload when unset; may OOM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid "`memory`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:0
msgid ""
"Favors lower GPU memory. Uses component offload, or Wan/MOVA layerwise DiT "
"offload when supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:33
msgid ""
"`auto` checks selected GPU memory before applying FSDP. In multi-GPU runs it "
"uses the least available memory across selected GPUs, and only turns on FSDP "
"automatically when doing so can replace DiT offload. Text encoder, image "
"encoder, and other component residency still follow the offload policy "
"unless the model marks a high-memory resident path as safe. When the model "
"default uses CFG and the user did not set a parallelism policy, `auto` may "
"also enable CFG parallelism. `speed` intentionally does not check memory; it "
"is the mode for users who prefer latency/throughput and accept OOM risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:35
msgid ""
"The modes tune residency for native pipeline components declared to the "
"component residency manager. Today this covers the major DiT, text/image "
"encoder, VAE, vocoder, and upsampler components; DiT can use layerwise "
"offload when supported, while text encoders use either resident execution or "
"component CPU offload. Do not assume text-encoder layerwise offload unless a "
"model implements and validates it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:37
msgid ""
"NOTE: The preset is intentionally coarse. A future continuous value such as "
"`0.0` to `1.0` could express the speed-memory tradeoff more precisely, but "
"it would need model-specific memory models and clearer user expectations. "
"Until then, use the preset plus explicit flags for overrides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:40
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:42
msgid ""
"sglang generate \\\n"
"  --model-path Qwen/Qwen-Image \\\n"
"  --num-gpus 2 \\\n"
"  --performance-mode auto\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:49
msgid ""
"sglang generate \\\n"
"  --model-path Wan-AI/Wan2.1-T2V-1.3B-Diffusers \\\n"
"  --performance-mode memory\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:55
msgid "Explicit flags win over the mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:57
msgid ""
"sglang generate \\\n"
"  --model-path Qwen/Qwen-Image \\\n"
"  --num-gpus 2 \\\n"
"  --performance-mode auto \\\n"
"  --use-fsdp-inference false\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:65
msgid ""
"In this example, `auto` will not re-enable FSDP. The same applies to "
"parallelism; for example, `--enable-cfg-parallel false` keeps CFG "
"parallelism disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:67
msgid "Interpreting The Levers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:69
msgid ""
"**No offload** keeps model components resident on GPU. It is usually fastest "
"when memory is sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:71
msgid ""
"**Component CPU offload** lowers GPU memory by moving large components to "
"CPU. It is simple and robust, but it usually trades latency for memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:73
msgid ""
"**Layerwise DiT offload** lowers DiT memory further for supported Wan/MOVA "
"models by moving DiT layers between CPU and GPU. It can be the best single-"
"GPU memory mode, but may increase latency and lower throughput."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:75
msgid ""
"**FSDP** shards DiT weights across multiple GPUs and all-gathers weights "
"during forward. It can reduce DiT CPU offload cost on multi-GPU deployments, "
"especially for validated Wan I2V workloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:77
msgid ""
"FSDP sharding granularity matters. SGLang Diffusion prefers sharding direct "
"repeated transformer block entries such as `transformer_blocks.0` or "
"`blocks.0`. Coarser sharding lowers wrapper count but can increase all-"
"gather peak memory; finer sharding can reduce transient memory but adds "
"communication and scheduling overhead. If a model does not define an "
"explicit sharding rule, the loader falls back to repeated block class names "
"and common direct numbered block paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:79
msgid ""
"**CFG parallelism** splits positive and negative CFG branches across GPUs. "
"For Qwen/Wan workloads with normal step counts, this is the most reliable "
"multi-GPU speedup observed so far."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:81
msgid ""
"**SP/Ulysses/Ring** splits sequence work. It can help video workloads, but "
"validated Qwen/Wan runs showed CFG parallelism outperforming SP for latency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:83
msgid ""
"**TP** is supported for compatibility and some model structures, but current "
"measurements do not make it the default latency path for Qwen/Wan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:85
msgid "Current Benchmark Takeaways"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:87
msgid "Observed regular-scale trends:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:89
msgid ""
"Z-Image: single-GPU no-offload was faster than FSDP/SP in the tested "
"setting; keep FSDP off unless memory or parallelism requires it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:90
msgid ""
"Qwen-Image: keep the default non-FSDP path unless a specific FSDP/SP/Ring "
"setting has been benchmarked on the target hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:91
msgid ""
"Wan: FSDP can replace DiT offload on validated multi-GPU workloads, while "
"text/image encoders may still need component offload. Keep model-specific "
"precision checks before making FSDP automatic for a path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:92
msgid ""
"Component offload mainly reduced memory; it did not improve latency in the "
"tested no-offload-vs-offload runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../diffusion/performance/deployment_cookbook.md:94
msgid ""
"Always benchmark with your actual resolution, frame count, step count, and "
"GPU type before locking production defaults."
msgstr ""
